
=head1 PAGINATORS

Paginator methods are helpers that repetively call methods that return partial results

[%- FOR op IN c.paginators_struct.keys.sort %]
[%- op_name = op %]
[%- paginator = c.paginators_struct.$op %]
[%- out_shape = c.input_for_operation(op_name) %]
[%- req_list = out_shape.required.sort %]
[%- opt_list = c.optional_params_in_shape(out_shape) %]

=head2 [% c.get_paginator_name(op) %]

  # Accumulate mode (all results in memory)
  my $result = $service->[% c.get_paginator_name(op) %]([%- FOREACH out_name IN req_list.sort -%]
  [%- member = c.shape(out_shape.members.$out_name.shape) -%]
  [%- out_name %] => $value[%- IF (NOT loop.last) %], [% END %]
[%- END %][%- IF (opt_list.size > 0) %][%- IF (req_list.size > 0) %], [% END %]...[% END %]);

  # Callback mode (per-element streaming)
  $service->[% c.get_paginator_name(op) %](sub { my ($item, $key) = @_; ... }[%- IF (req_list.size > 0) %], [% END -%]
[%- FOREACH out_name IN req_list.sort -%]
  [%- member = c.shape(out_shape.members.$out_name.shape) -%]
  [%- out_name %] => $value[%- IF (NOT loop.last) %], [% END %]
[%- END %][%- IF (opt_list.size > 0) %][%- IF (req_list.size > 0) %], [% END %]...[% END %]);

  # Iterator mode (lazy per-page)
  my $paginator = $service->[% c.get_paginator_name(op) %]({ iterator => 1 }[%- IF (req_list.size > 0) %], [% END -%]
[%- FOREACH out_name IN req_list.sort -%]
  [%- member = c.shape(out_shape.members.$out_name.shape) -%]
  [%- out_name %] => $value[%- IF (NOT loop.last) %], [% END %]
[%- END %][%- IF (opt_list.size > 0) %][%- IF (req_list.size > 0) %], [% END %]...[% END %]);
  while (my $page = $paginator->next_page) { ... }

=head3 Pagination modes

This paginator supports three modes of operation:

=head4 Accumulate mode (default)

Fetches all pages and returns a single response with merged result keys. B<Warning>: this can consume large amounts of memory for big result sets.

  my $result = $service->[% c.get_paginator_name(op) %](
[%- FOREACH out_name IN req_list.sort -%]
  [%- member = c.shape(out_shape.members.$out_name.shape) -%]
    [%- out_name %] => [% c.perl_type_to_pod(member.perl_type) %],
[%- END %]
  );

=head4 Callback mode

Pass a coderef as the first argument to process each element as it arrives. The callback receives the element as the first parameter and the result key name as the second:

[%- FOREACH param = c.paginator_result_key(paginator) %]

 - C<[% param %]>: callback receives each element from this key, with C<'[% param %]'> as the second argument

[%- END %]

  $service->[% c.get_paginator_name(op) %](
    sub {
      my ($element, $key_name) = @_;
      # process $element
    },
[%- FOREACH out_name IN req_list.sort %]
[%- member = c.shape(out_shape.members.$out_name.shape) %]
    [% out_name %] => [% c.perl_type_to_pod(member.perl_type) %],
[%- END %]
  );

=head4 Iterator mode

Pass C<{ iterator =E<gt> 1 }> as the first argument to get a L<Paws::API::Paginator> object. Each call to C<next_page()> fetches exactly one page. To stop early, simply stop calling C<next_page()>.

  my $paginator = $service->[% c.get_paginator_name(op) %](
    { iterator => 1 },
[%- FOREACH out_name IN req_list.sort %]
[%- member = c.shape(out_shape.members.$out_name.shape) %]
    [% out_name %] => [% c.perl_type_to_pod(member.perl_type) %],
[%- END %]
  );

  while (my $page = $paginator->next_page) {
    # $page is [% out_shape = c.shapename_for_operation_output(op_name); IF (out_shape) %]a L<[% c.api %]::[% out_shape %]> instance[% ELSE %]a response object[% END %]
    last if $done;  # early break
  }

  # or check explicitly:
  if ($paginator->has_next_page) { ... }

[%- IF (paginator.limit_key.defined) %]

=head3 Controlling page size

Use C<[% paginator.limit_key %]> to control how many results the service returns per page. This applies to all three pagination modes:

  # Accumulate with page size
  my $result = $service->[% c.get_paginator_name(op) %](
[%- FOREACH out_name IN req_list.sort %]
[%- member = c.shape(out_shape.members.$out_name.shape) %]
    [% out_name %] => [% c.perl_type_to_pod(member.perl_type) %],
[%- END %]
    [% paginator.limit_key %] => 100,
  );

  # Iterator with page size
  my $paginator = $service->[% c.get_paginator_name(op) %](
    { iterator => 1 },
[%- FOREACH out_name IN req_list.sort %]
[%- member = c.shape(out_shape.members.$out_name.shape) %]
    [% out_name %] => [% c.perl_type_to_pod(member.perl_type) %],
[%- END %]
    [% paginator.limit_key %] => 100,
  );

[%- END %]

[% END %]

